# The Flooded Nave - the Drowned Abbess's arena (location 190, BOSS_ARENA, AL 12; NaveLevel;
# docs/arch/40-m4-design.md section 6.1)
#
# A drowned abbey church, entered from the Crypts' last stair (the arrival, bottom centre) or through
# the nave doors on the west wall (out to the overworld mouth at (9,9)). North: the chancel with the
# altar dais, where the Abbess kneels, and the fallen bell behind it. Between: the crossing (band 3),
# then the nave - eleven rows of pews (passable, never flood) split by the central aisle (band 1) and
# the two side aisles (band 2), with pillars that break the line of sight; south: the narthex (band 4).
#
# Tide (phase 2): every 6 turns the next band (1 -> 4) becomes deep water. Pews, plinths, the dais and
# the plain floor never flood. Candles (c) stand on plinths; a lit candle shelters its 3x3 from the toll.
# NaveRules (checked at load and by NaveTest / MapSourceTest): dry cells >= 30% of the walkable floor at
# full tide; every dry cell reaches the dais over dry cells, wading at most 2 deep cells at a time; a
# lit square within 8 steps of every dry cell; the arrival and the doors dry.
#
# The rood line (marker rood): the fight starts when the hero first stands on or north of it.
#
# Format: world/MapSource (arch 10 section 3.4; 'tide:<n>' and 'candle' are the arena features).

kind arena
size 21 22
scale 1
seed 0

legend
  # WALL
  . EMPTY
  d EMPTY_SP feature:dais             # the altar dais (never floods)
  A EMPTY_SP feature:dais @abbess     # where she kneels
  B STATUE feature:bell               # the fallen bell
  c EMPTY_SP candle                   # a candle stand on its plinth
  T EMPTY_DECO feature:pew            # pews: passable, never flood
  O WALL feature:pillar               # pillars block sight
  1 WATER tide:1                      # the central aisle
  2 WATER tide:2                      # the side aisles
  3 WATER tide:3                      # the crossing
  4 WATER tide:4                      # the narthex
  @ ENTRANCE @arrival                 # up the stair to the Crypts' last floor
  D EXIT @doors                       # the nave doors: out to the overworld mouth
  = EMPTY @threshold
end

